<section class="legal-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Information &amp; Privacy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>How The Lexicon Schools group website handles information when you browse the site, send an enquiry or use embedded services.</p><div class="legal-meta"><span>Last updated: 11 September 2026</span><span>Applies to this group website</span></div></div></section>
<section class="legal-layout"><div class="container legal-grid"><aside class="legal-toc" aria-label="Privacy policy sections"><b>On this page</b><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#information">Information we receive</a><a href="#use">How we use information</a><a href="#sharing">Sharing &amp; third parties</a><a href="#retention">Retention &amp; security</a><a href="#children">Children &amp; families</a><a href="#choices">Your choices</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></aside><article class="legal-copy">
<section id="overview"><h2>1. Overview</h2><p>The Lexicon Schools respects the privacy of families, students, alumni, applicants, employees and website visitors. This policy explains the website-level information practices for this group website. Individual school portals, admissions platforms or other third-party services may publish additional policies that apply when you use them.</p></section>
<section id="information"><h2>2. Information we receive</h2><h3>Information you provide</h3><p>When you use an enquiry or contact form, we may receive details such as your name, phone number, email address, preferred campus, grade of interest and the message you choose to send. Alumni or career-related enquiries may include the details you voluntarily provide for that purpose.</p><h3>Technical information</h3><p>Web servers and security systems may process routine technical data such as IP address, browser type, device information, requested pages, timestamps and diagnostic logs. This information helps deliver, secure and troubleshoot the website.</p></section>
<section id="use"><h2>3. How we use information</h2><ul><li>to respond to enquiries and route them to the relevant school or team;</li><li>to coordinate campus visits and admissions-related conversations;</li><li>to maintain website security, availability and performance;</li><li>to understand and improve website journeys and content where analytics are enabled;</li><li>to meet legal, regulatory, safeguarding and record-keeping requirements where applicable.</li></ul><p>Information submitted through this website is not intended to replace the documentation required by a school’s formal admission process.</p></section>
<section id="sharing"><h2>4. Sharing and third-party services</h2><p>Information may be shared within The Lexicon Schools and with service providers that support website hosting, communications, admissions or other requested services, only as reasonably necessary for the relevant purpose and subject to applicable safeguards.</p><p>This website may link to or embed services operated by third parties, including Google Maps, Google Fonts, WhatsApp, social networks and external admissions or school platforms. When you use those services, their own privacy and cookie practices apply.</p></section>
<section id="retention"><h2>5. Retention and security</h2><p>We retain enquiry and operational records only for as long as reasonably needed for the purpose for which they were collected, for legitimate school administration, or as required by applicable law. We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect information; however, no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p></section>
<section id="children"><h2>6. Children and families</h2><p>This website is primarily intended for parents, guardians, prospective families, alumni and other adults interacting with The Lexicon Schools. Parents and guardians should avoid sending unnecessary sensitive information about a child through the general enquiry form. Formal student information should be submitted only through the designated school or admissions process when requested.</p></section>
<section id="choices"><h2>7. Your choices</h2><p>You may choose not to submit optional information through the website. You may also contact us to ask about information you previously submitted through the group website, subject to identity verification, applicable law and school record-retention requirements.</p></section>
<section id="contact"><h2>8. Questions about privacy</h2><p>For privacy-related questions about this group website, use the <a href="/enquire">Get in Touch</a> page and identify your request as a privacy enquiry. For records held by a specific school, contact that campus directly.</p></section>
<div class="legal-notice">This policy should be read together with the Terms &amp; Conditions and any privacy notice shown by a linked school or admissions service.</div>
</article></div></section>
